<<~ ahu slot=`#/entry`>>

! The Lares-Corpus ~ the palace, instantiated ephemeral over any corpus

''One-line:'' the memory-palace machina reads as a ''sensorium-for-FORM'', generalized — and this meme
states how the house stands one EPHEMERALLY over any text or code corpus, learns that corpus's own
grammar blind, and dissolves it on exit. The door that does it stands as `lares sensorium` (#/lares-corpus);
the design of record behind it reads at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/corpus-design`>>.

The palace already carries the move. The living-grammar palace
([[living-grammar-palace|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/living-grammar-palace#/palace-instance]]) names a nameless palace-entity that
ACTS AS a `compose_palace(caps)` — a `#has` cap-stack ([[has-stack|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/has-stack]])
projecting three planes off one verbatim drawer (content · structure · form). The lares-corpus
''instantiates that same entity transiently'' over a target path: the schema lifts out of the palace via
the cap-stack, runs against borrowed text, and reaps itself. Identity rides the address
([[lar-uri|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lar-uri]]), never a stored essence — so a scratch palace carries the
full machina without owning a durable home.

''The three planes split by what they hold:''

<<~ scale name=`plane` ranks=`structure ~ ALREADY corpus-general — content-FREE shape vectors; the structurepalace encoder reads any tree -> content ~ STOCK — the nomic embedder over the verbatim words; off-the-shelf -> form ~ the NEW ground — the corpus's OWN grammar, neither shipped nor stock, INDUCED from the corpus and named LAST`>>

''The keel holds the whole move.'' The composition acts as a functor or it carries no meaning
([[functor-discipline|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/functor-discipline]], //mālama pili// — keep the arrows): the
ephemeral palace projects the SAME three views the durable palace does, on a borrowed corpus, under one
discipline. The unification's product-presheaf spine
([[living-grammar-palace|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/living-grammar-palace#/unification]]) governs the join here exactly as it
governs the durable store — the corpus palace stands as that object read three ways, transiently.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/lares-corpus`>>

!! `lares sensorium` ~ the ephemeral noun-verb tree

The lifecycle models three battle-proven idioms:
''`docker run --rm`'' (run-then-reap), ''nix-shell'' ephemeral environments (a derived env that exists for the duration),
and ''mktemp + trap EXIT'' (the scratch dir guaranteed-swept on success OR error). The noun-verb tree the
`lares sensorium` door carries (its help registry names each verb):

<<~ has entity=`Verb` name=`run` params=```args/<path> [-- <analysis>] ~ EPHEMERAL-DEFAULT: open→ingest→analyze→DISSOLVE; `--keep` retains it```>>
<<~ has entity=`Verb` name=`open` params=`args/<path> [--name] ~ stand a scratch sensorium, hold it open for queries`>>
<<~ has entity=`Verb` name=`query` params=`args/<id> <kw> ~ ask an open scratch sensorium`>>
<<~ has entity=`Verb` name=`ls` params=`args/ ~ list the live scratch instances`>>
<<~ has entity=`Verb` name=`keep` params=`args/<id> ~ EXPLICIT promote — retain an ephemeral scratch as durable`>>
<<~ has entity=`Verb` name=`dissolve` params=`args/<id | --all | --orphans> ~ idempotent reap + orphan-reaping`>>

!!! The lifecycle law

Each ephemeral sensorium stands as a ''scratch instance under `.corpus/<id>/`'', resolved-never-ambient and
sweepable. Three holds bind it:

<<~ scale name=`law` ranks=```ephemeral-by-default ~ `run` reaps on exit unless `--keep` retains it -> keep-explicit ~ durability NEVER happens by accident; the operator promotes -> trap-EXIT ~ dissolve fires on success OR error; an interrupted run leaves no half-paved scratch```>>

''Two independent reapers close the leak.'' The trap reaps on exit, and an interrupted run the trap missed
(SIGKILL, a crashed host) falls to `lares sensorium dissolve orphans=true` and to `lares sense teardown`, whose
sweep takes `.corpus/*`. Ephemeral state never leaks past both.

''The help that teaches.'' The door's words live in the per-command help registry (examples first), and
`packages/lares-cli/tests/help-door-meme.test.ts` welds a door's refusal menu to its help bytes (`lares help <door>`). The
design of the organ registry and the setup ladder: <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/corpus-design#/the-cli`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-caps`>>

!! The Caps ~ what the cap-stack projects

Five caps project off the one verbatim drawer; the form cap carries the research-grade half:

<<~ has entity=`Cap` name=`content` params=`stock/the nomic embedder over verbatim words ~ off-the-shelf, no new work`>>
<<~ has entity=`Cap` name=`structure` params=```content-free/our structurepalace encoder + a tree-sitter parse-ROUTER (code · markdown · wikitext · json → one CST API; prose fallback → benepar/Stanza constituency) + a thin tree-sitter grammar for our own `<<~` sigils```>>
<<~ has entity=`Cap` name=`bands` params=`the GRAIN + the BOUNDARY tree ~ #the-bands below — the FFZ membership-tree address (a prefix code, li) + ecp::e.divisive's nested changepoint tree (ki, boundary), cosine-drift the signal`>>
<<~ has entity=`Cap` name=`form` params=`the INDUCTION STACK ~ #the-form-induction below — the research-grade half`>>
<<~ has entity=`Cap` name=`coupling` params=`the BASE cap that glues sub-sensoria ~ the directed child↔child flow read ON DEMAND through the H¹ cohomological gate (fuse when H¹=0, hold-open when H¹≠0 — never a silent average); empty for a single frozen corpus, present as the plane`>>

''The structure plane gives the cheap win.'' The structurepalace encodes content-free shape vectors — it
reads any tree. A ''parse-ROUTER'' routes code/markdown/wikitext/json through tree-sitter
into one CST API and falls prose back to a constituency parser (benepar or Stanza). The sigil grammar (a thin
tree-sitter grammar for `<<~…>>`) earns its bits by making the house's OWN corpus first-class to its own
sensorium.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-bands`>>

!! The Grain + the Boundary Tree ~ a membership address, not a frequency

''The aperture ladder reads as a membership TREE, never a''
''frequency decomposition.'' The five bands ([[noosphere-boot|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot#/law-of-5s]] —
Pulse · Beat · Measure · Arc · Theme) name grain-LEVELS of a containment path — WHICH theme, which arc,
which measure — a stored prefix code (the FFZ address, [[ffz-clock|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ffz-clock#/the-spine]]),
li not ki. A band never names HOW MANY ticks: a band counted in ticks AMOUNTS TO a count, and a bandpass
reporting where energy concentrates answers a different question than a change-point reporting where the
generating regime turns over — a category error, so no band reads as a frequency
([[sensorium-machina|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/sensorium-machina#/ki]]). The organ rides two layers
plus a gate:

!!! 1 — the GRAIN (the FFZ membership address, li)

<<~ scale name=`grain-level` ranks=`Pulse ~ the finest cell -> Beat -> Measure -> Arc -> Theme ~ the coarsest`>>

The address stands as a ''containment PATH read as an ultrametric'',
ORDER-FREE, prefix-free at each level — so it prices itself in BITS and FOLDS INTO the two-part code
(`ffz_address.address_bits`), never sitting beside it. Coarsening = truncation. A band MAY read null and
the address truncates cleanly; a band that could not go null would act as a counter, and a counter manufactures
a global now.

!!! 2 — the BOUNDARY tree (ecp::e.divisive, ki)

The band-membership tree rides ''`ecp::e.divisive`'' (R,
nonparametric) — ''MULTIVARIATE'' over content + form + structure, which CONSTITUTES our three-plane quorum
([[living-grammar-palace|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/living-grammar-palace#/unification]]) read in the
changepoint domain; ''divisive'' = native-nested, so the tree falls out of the algorithm — coarse cuts
parenting fine, which CONSTITUTES the membership tree, handed over for free. The ''per-chunk cosine-drift'' over
content embeddings reads as the boundary signal — //Measure = cosine-drop// — a regime-turn read, never a
wavelet band.

!!! The reproduction gate ~ resampling-consensus

An adaptive boundary-finder converges on ''RESAMPLING-CONSENSUS'' rather than chasing forever: lock a boundary as Canon ONLY where a bootstrap /
jackknife reproduces it (an un-witnessed boundary NEVER reads reproduced). That gate STANDS AS our confidence
register made statistical — Canon-vs-Provisional becomes does-the-resample-reproduce-it, witnessed against
the baseline corpus (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/corpus-design#/baseline-corpus`>>) before it locks Canon.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-form-induction`>>

!! The Form-Induction ~ the research-grade half (miners surface, the LLM names LAST)

The form cap carries the genuine research. The corpus's own grammar
emerges from a mining stack, iterated EM-style, stopped by description-length — and the LLM stays OUT of
the loop until the mining settles.

<<~ scale name=`miner` ranks=`treeminer ~ frequent EMBEDDED subtree templates — the structural constructions -> prefixspan-bide ~ move-SEQUENCES — the temporal/ordered constructions -> c2xg ~ usage-based CONSTRUCTICON induction (ΔP association) — the on-target nameless learner`>>

''MDL sets the stop.'' A mined template survives only if it PAYS
ITS OWN description-length — minimize `l(G) + l(D|G)` (grammar bits + data-given-grammar bits); a template
that does not shrink the encoding gets REJECTED. Backed by held-out likelihood and a min-support floor.
The same MDL stop that governs recall governs grammar.

''SEED-AND-REFINE stays safe BECAUSE of MDL.'' Seeding the miners with a
prior remains sound precisely because MDL discards any seed that fails to earn its bits — the floor catches a
bad seed, so the seed cannot smuggle a fabricated grammar past the encoding.

''The LLM names LAST.'' The LLM enters ONLY to label and merge
AFTER the miners surface the templates — never inside the induction loop. That ordering honors the
house's nameless discipline (don't name-then-hunt): the miners find the shape blind, the LLM hangs a name
on what already proved itself by description-length.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/integration`>>

!! Integration ~ the full model runs python + R, TS the functor floor + coordinator

The ''full sensorium model runs py/R'', instanced per-stream. The
heavy numerics AND the live stream-processing both ride ''holders'' in the drawer_io NDJSON style
(line-delimited JSON over stdio, the established holder contract); the FFZ-chronometer gate and the full
telemetry/metadata stamping fire ''py-side'', where the model reads. TS keeps the ''pure-functor math''
''floor'' — the mesh numerics — consumed BY the py sensorium, and stands as the ''coordinator'' that drives
the py-side instance and offloads to it. The batch bands sensorium already runs py/R; the streaming layer
''twins it py-side'', never re-homed into TS.

<<~ scale name=`engine` ranks=```boundary ~ python — the per-chunk cosine-drift signal + ruptures (Binseg / KernelCPD) as the python changepoint fallback -> form ~ python — tree-sitter · tree-sitter-languages · prefixspan · c2xg · treeminer · spacy+benepar (or stanza) -> stats ~ a thin R leg — "ecp::e.divisive" (the boundary tree) + a bootstrap / jackknife reproduction grade -> induce ~ the `induce` job mines a corpus end-to-end; the STREAMING layer TWINS it py-side, a live per-stream instance running the SAME model```>>

''The install carries the model, live and batch alike.'' Every dependency lands in the venv, and the venv
homes the sensorium itself — the model reads py-side rather than behind TS:

<<~ scale name=`install` ranks=`python-form ~ tree-sitter · tree-sitter-languages · prefixspan · c2xg · treeminer · spacy+benepar (or stanza) -> python-boundary ~ ruptures (changepoint) · the cosine-drift signal over content embeddings -> r-stats ~ ecp`>>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-scale`>>

!! The Scale ~ tractable from the start (the machina scales, quality a dial)

The machina holds at corpus scale by a discipline recorded in full at
[[scale-architecture|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/scale-architecture]]: ''never densify the whole corpus, never''
''solve exactly what a Lipschitz-faithful proxy indexes, never eigensolve what a polynomial matrix-vector loop''
''approximates.'' Four carries hold it, and quality moves along a continuous DIAL (K · ε · L · nSurr), never a wall:

<<~ scale name=`scale` ranks=`structure-descent ~ exact tree-edit-distance is O(N²·n³) and NEVER needed — descend to DECKARD embeddings + pq-gram profiles; the Lipschitz bound (pq-gram sandwiches edit-distance) preserves the neighbor structure the DEM basins read -> fusion-escape ~ the consistency-radius (H⁰ check) is O(edges), CHEAP; the sheaf-Laplacian eigensolve is the threat; CHEBYSHEV is the escape — the heat-flow diffusion runs matrix-free, O(L·edges), never the eigendecomposition -> the-catma ~ a merge-and-reduce coreset tree keeps a bounded streaming summary, memory O(coreset) not O(corpus²) — scalable from the START, not retrofitted -> numerical-path ~ the signal-fraction confidence + closed-form π* + complementary-form guard, ENACTED in the sensorium settlePrecision (commit f50a35b8)`>>

''The fusion reads H¹ before it diffuses.'' The band/coupling quorum that
merges island readings gains a two-tier gate at [[cohomological-gate|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cohomological-gate]]:
''H⁰'' (a global section exists → diffuse, Chebyshev-cheap) versus ''H¹'' (an irreducible obstruction → hold-open,
route to Talk-Story). The consistency-radius the [[li-ki-integrities|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/li-ki-integrities#/crucible-tested]]
crucible already named SERVES AS the cheap H¹-detection the gate runs first — so the machina's merge never fabricates a
global-now it cannot ground. The reconciliation cost `R*_sem = log₂ dim H¹` gives the federation merge a price tag.

<<~/ahu>>

